$DIR/test.p:37:26: cannot index B: methods Index and SetIndex use different key or element types
    The indexing methods of one type must agree: Index, SetIndex and IndexOk
    take the same key type K, and use the same element type V. Otherwise x[k]
    would have a different type depending on whether it is read or assigned, and
    x[k] += 1 could not read and write the same element.
    (see "Indexing library containers" in the Plutonium spec, section 11.11)
    (run "pluto explain E2453" for a longer explanation)
